# C2 gate walk (tools/check_fixture_equivalence.sh, inc-10v7f): a human warrior
# who takes the feats that open a sub-menu, SAVED at the end of creation with
# nothing played. Skill Focus opens the skill menu, Exotic Weapon the exotic
# weapon menu and Weapon Focus the weapon menu; the huge morningstar is too large
# for a human, so the game asks "Continue?" (Create.cpp CheckWeapon). Hits
# skill_focus, exotic_weapon, feat_weapon, weapon_unfit_confirm. Point buy keeps
# the rolled sets and their perks out of the character.
a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
@choose "Human"
@choose "Athletics"
@choose "Diplomacy"
@choose "Warrior"
p       # Attributes: abort to Point Buy
RIGHT*6 DOWN RIGHT*8 DOWN RIGHT*10 DOWN RIGHT*10 DOWN RIGHT*4 DOWN RIGHT*8 DOWN RIGHT*9
ENTER   # every point spent
y       # Are these your final stats? -- yes
@choose "Neutral"
@choose "Skill Focus"
@choose "Climb"
@choose "Exotic Weapon"
@choose "kukri"
TAB     # the next page of feats
@choose "Weapon Focus"
@choose "huge morningstar"
@while "too large for you" y      # too large to wield: the player goes on
@choose "long sword"            # the warrior's own focus pick: the same sub-menu again
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN   # spend every rank
@while "Unspent Skill Ranks" ENTER y   # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks
@while "wish to worship" y
@choose "The Ambitious Conqueror"
@until "System Menu" ESC
@expect "System Menu"
b       # [b] Save and Continue
@dump:saved
